WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.900
Yugi Muto assembled the Millennium Puzzle 
and became the guardian of the Shadow Games.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.260
Pegasus has a Millennium Item 
of his own - the Millennium Eye.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.800
Yugi accepts Pegasus's challenge 
and goes to Duelist Kingdom.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.940
Pegasus stole his grandfather Sugoroku's 
soul, and Yugi intends to rescue him.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.940
He battles alongside his trusted 
friends and with his other self.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.210
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.960
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.660
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.760
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:20.060
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.310
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.580
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.320
What is truly precious?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.460
Terror!
Call of the Haunted

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:30.560
Jonouchi, you'll never recover 
from your fear of dueling.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.600
What?

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.160
You're a loser dog!

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.100
Loser dog?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:44.030
Loser dog!

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.760
It was a dream.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.360
Dammit!  I'm not a loser!

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.360
It's morning!  Wake up!

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:12.800
You're full of spirit, Jonouchi.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.860
Yeah!  It's the second day of the tournament!

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.710
I'll gather more Star Chips so 
that I can enter Pegasus's castle!

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.130
Keep your voice down.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.250
You're all awake.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.700
Good morning, Anzu.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.130
Where's Mai Kujaku?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:31.830
Mai asked me to give this to you.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:37.960
This is an IOU for the Star Chips.  Kisses!

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.300
An IOU?

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.500
Mai wants to go at this alone.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.460
Are you ready?

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.000
Yeah.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.640
Yup.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.900
All right.  Let's go.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.660
How many duelists are left on the island?

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:05.420
Ten or so duelists were sent home yesterday.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.600
And the Player Killers must 
have eliminated others.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:15.000
That means out of the 40 participants, 
about half were eliminated.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.860
You still have time, Jonouchi.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.600
Keep on getting more Star Chips.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.530
But don't take too long.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.860
There's also a time limit.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.230
The remaining duelists must be powerful 
because they survived the first day.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.750
They're even stronger?

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.530
Yugi, you're scaring Jonouchi.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:40.400
I'm not scared!

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.930
Whattaya want?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.800
Stop fighting.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.500
No matter how powerful my 
opponent, I'll defeat 'em!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.150
That's the spirit, Jonouchi!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.300
How about them?

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.820
Let's finish them.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:04.130
But only two are wearing Duel Gloves.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.300
So the others are just observers.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:13.990
It's that Yugi kid.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.460
Yugi?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.930
Let's report this to the boss.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.160
Good idea.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.860
You found some prey?

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.860
Yeah.  Two more.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.800
But there's a small problem.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.930
We should forget about them.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.000
We may not be able to beat them.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.260
One of them is Yugi.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:40.160
He's already beaten Kaiba, and he'll 
certainly make it to the castle.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.940
Yugi?  Never heard of him.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:48.900
Besides, we're the ones who'll 
make it to the castle.

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:54.200
That's right.  That's why 
we made this alliance.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:01.730
I knew we'd win once we teamed up 
with a famous duelist like you.

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:11.280
That's right.  You weaklings have survived so far 
because you received advice from me, Bandit Keith.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:16.860
We have nothing to fear because the United 
States's top money earner is on our team!

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:20.030
Bandit Keith is on our side!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.840
That's right!

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.800
What?  Stop messing around, Pegasus!

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.330
I am not messing around.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:38.530
This boy will duel in my place.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.580
I play this card, kid!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.930
Umm...

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.250
If you play that card, I should play this.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.580
What?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.260
Tom wins.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.130
Just you wait, Pegasus.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:54.900
I'll get revenge for making a fool of me.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.730
What about the other one?

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.730
He looked pretty weak.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.500
Then let's get him.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:09.170
I haven't seen any duelists for a while.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.530
Maybe we walked too deep into the forest.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:17.580
Since there are fewer duelists, 
finding one is hard work.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.330
I'm taking a timeout.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.230
Wait for me here.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.130
What's up?

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.900
Nature calls.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:34.860
Boss, where are we going?

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.460
To a hidden stage.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:38.360
Hidden stage?

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.800
I found it by chance.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.420
Pegasus built a special 
stage inside this cave.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:56.160
Kotsuzuka, your deck is 
full of Ghost cards, right?

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.760
Yeah.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.390
Show me.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.520
This deck isn't strong enough.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.440
You think so?

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.140
Don't worry.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:17.360
I'll add my cards to build 
the strongest Ghost deck.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.880
Just ahead is the Graveyard field.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.230
Graveyard field?

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.630
Bring our prey there.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.900
With these Ghost cards, 
there's no way you'll lose.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:34.660
Understood.  Leave it to me.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.200
I'm counting on you.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.500
You better get me to Pegasus's castle.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.200
Don't be scared.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.100
It's fake.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.580
Pegasus has bad taste.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.550
Wait for me!

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.230
That was refreshing.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.030
Who are you?

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:15.740
How dare you...

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:23.940
Wake up!

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.060
It's you!

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.020
You're finally awake.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.460
Who are you?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.200
This is your graveyard.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.520
Duel, standby!

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:34.150
What?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.360
What is this place?

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.830
A cross?

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:54.230
Welcome to the Graveyard field.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:10:00.350
I will bury you.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.900
It's a ghost!

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:19.330
Jonouchi is taking a long time.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.600
He sure is.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.730
I wonder if he got lost.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.930
Maybe someone challenged him to a duel.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.200
That's a possibility.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:33.530
Jonouchi would love to surprise us 
by secretly winning some Star Chips.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.060
Let's split up and search for him.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:38.530
Bakura and I will go this way.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.200
Yugi and Anzu, go that way.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.160
Okay.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:47.860
It's time to duel.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:51.130
This is your graveyard.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.000
He's scary.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.430
He sure is.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:02.140
Look at him.  He fainted 
while he's still standing.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:04.830
How pathetic.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:06.800
Wake him up.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:09.080
Wake up already!

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:13.600
You fainted when you saw the Graveyard field?

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:17.760
You're the biggest coward I've ever met.

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:19.930
The Graveyard field?

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.430
Evil spirits haunt this underground cave.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.430
You can't escape.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:32.170
I didn't faint because I 
saw the Graveyard field.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:35.040
I fainted because you're so creepy!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.530
He has a point, Kotsuzuka.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:42.760
You look like a ghost in this cave.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.050
Be quiet!  It's due to the candlelight!

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:50.200
We'll both wager all our Star Chips.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.360
Bring out your four Star Chips.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:55.560
I don't get a say in this duel?

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.960
Well?  Are you dueling or not?

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.570
In this crazy place?

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:06.930
You're scared.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:11.360
The battle hasn't started yet, but 
you already look like a loser dog.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.700
Loser dog?

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:21.320
You're a loser dog that's afraid to duel.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.830
I'll duel you!

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.160
If I run away, I'll really be a loser.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.900
I'll face you!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.230
Duel!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.680
Kotsuzuka, use your Ghost 
cards to bury him quickly.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.760
Ghost cards?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.680
I now understand.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:56.060
You finally realized that the 
Duel Ring is 100% Graveyard.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.930
My Ghost cards will power up.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:02.930
Jonouchi!

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:06.070
He's not over here.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:07.930
Let's look over there.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:12.900
Jonouchi!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:14.730
It's no good.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:19.080
It's weird.  We should be able to 
find him if he's at a Duel Ring.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:22.680
Where did Jonouchi go?

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:31.680
Here I go.  I play my Ghost card-

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.310
Stop!

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.260
Don't play that card, Kotsuzuka.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:38.800
Play the leftmost card.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:41.100
The leftmost card?

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.800
Zanki?

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.400
But this isn't a Ghost card.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.880
I put that card into your deck.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:55.060
If I play this card, it 
won't gain any Field Power.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.880
You'll be fine if you do what I tell you.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.230
But...

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.400
Kotsuzuka, do what he says.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.190
We've survived this far by 
listening to his advice.

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:11.730
Stop discussing with the peanut gallery!

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:13.900
Fine.  I'll trust you.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:17.230
I play Zanki in attack position!

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:24.100
In that case, I'll play this card.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.330
Axe Raider attacks!

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:29.850
Gale Slice!

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:39.430
Yeah!  I destroyed Zanki!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.700
He destroyed it.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:44.200
It's fine.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:47.330
That card was a lame Warrior.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:51.700
If I played a Ghost card, 
it wouldn't have lost.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:56.340
Oh yeah!  You can rest in peace 
because there are plenty of graves!

00:14:56.340 --> 00:15:00.680
Play your next card, creep.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.820
I'll definitely play a Ghost card this time.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.000
Kotsuzuka, not that one.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.830
The second one from the left.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.400
This is Crawling Dragon.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:14.460
This isn't one of my Ghost cards either.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:18.540
It'll be destroyed as soon as I play it.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:23.660
Don't worry.  You'll win using my strategy.

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:27.470
Trust the mind of an undefeated duelist.

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.480
Fine.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.640
I play this in defense position.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:34.400
You're running scared.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.780
You're nothing special.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.560
Axe Raider, destroy it!

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.800
All right!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.230
Next, play the rightmost card.

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:56.000
Don't place it in defense position this time.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:00.170
He might not attack if he 
can't see your monster.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:05.260
If you won't trust me, 
I'll stop giving advice.

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.830
It's up to you.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.700
I play Crass Clown in attack position!

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.760
I play this card.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.030
Flame Swordsman!

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.560
Battle!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.440
Flaming Battle Sword!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:38.240
Yeah!  Crass Clown is destroyed.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.980
I'm going to win.

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:51.700
Until now, I've been irritated with myself 
because I've always needed Yugi's help.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:55.740
But now, I'm winning on my own.

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.400
Just watch, Kaiba.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:17:01.470
I'll prove that I'm no loser!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:05.200
Boss.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:09.940
Don't worry.  You've already won this duel.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:13.180
You're always whispering to each other.

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:17.000
If you want, I'll take you all on!

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:21.300
Really?  Then Kotsuzuka, it's time to do it.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:31.260
I now understand.  You wanted me 
to turn the tables with this card.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.000
You're incredible.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.400
Show him your trump card!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:39.430
Prepare yourself!  This 
is my special spell card!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.880
Call of the Haunted!

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.280
Call of the Haunted?

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.880
All monsters in the graveyard 
resurrect as Zombies.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:53.960
Zombies are Ghost cards that are immortal.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.830
What?

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.260
That's Jonouchi's...

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:12.940
This is Jonouchi's little sister?

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:18.200
As absent-minded as he is, he'll 
never lose something this important.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.030
Something must have happened to him.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.450
Look!

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.150
Is he inside?

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.830
What's this?

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:41.800
Be careful.  This is no ordinary cave.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:44.700
Are those coffins?

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.970
But they're fake.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:50.400
Leave them alone.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.530
They're creepy.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.160
There's nothing to be worried about.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:03.160
Take this!

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.700
Stop!

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:09.730
Pegasus is playing a prank.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:11.400
Jonouchi...

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.030
What's with them?

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:25.730
Call of the Haunted turned all 
the monsters into Zombies.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:26.850
Zombies?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:32.360
Since they're now Ghost cards, they 
gain power from the Graveyard field.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:42.160
Dragon Zombie, attack Axe Raider!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:46.000
Counterattack, Axe Raider!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:53.300
Impossible!  He scored a clean 
hit, but it returned to normal!

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.610
Since Zombies are immortal, 
they can keep resurrecting.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:58.940
What?

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:02.400
Go!  Dragon Zombie attacks!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:05.160
Zombie Deadly Breath!

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:26.900
They're too dangerous!

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:35.980
Ghost Kotsuzuka's Zombie monsters 
are roughing up Jonouchi.

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:40.690
They not only keep resurrecting, 
but they also keep powering up!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:47.790
Time Wizard has pulled him out of trouble 
many times before, but it failed this time!

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:51.700
Don't give up, Jonouchi!  You're not a loser!

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:55.530
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Shield & Sword

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.300
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:09.560
The flask glistens

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:17.410
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:26.380
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:34.160
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:39.990
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:44.100
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:52.370
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:56.610
Shower of happiness

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:00.740
You are not alone

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:07.460
You're protected by a 
giant ring of friendship
